    {
      "id": "MIN-02",
      "title": "A special value controls each character length",
      "statement": "For ℓ odd and ℓ∤n, the minus length is finite and its product with log ℓ is at most the sum of the negative logarithms of p-adic norms of integral, parity-matched primitive Bernoulli values. The selected supplier is ML.iv on Poitou–Tate duality and unramified orthogonality.",
