    {
      "id": "MIN-03",
      "title": "One rational integer for all non-degree primes",
      "statement": "For k=j+1 the parity-selected product is a nonzero integer, uniform in coefficient fields. Its logarithmic size is at most n log(16 N^(k+1) k!). Prime valuations of that integer bound every finite set of odd primes prime to the degree at once. The j-sum is bounded by 3nt²log(tN).",
