    {
      "id": "MIN-04",
      "title": "Torsion exponent and generator count at exceptional primes",
      "statement": "An integral higher Stickelberger operator kills φ(Nℓ) times each kernel class. Its signed determinant and the valuation of φ(Nℓ) produce a power ℓ^r killing the minus part with r log ℓ≤30n(j+1)log(jℓN). Torsion length at level one is ≤8ℓn log(ℓN). Multiplying gives the admissible constant 240.",
